1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
[Machine transcript — not human reviewed]
So you have to die.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:10,200
KILLING MOTHER
A live performance document

3
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,260
Do all of you want me to die?

4
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:13,240
[Fragment] You.

5
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:15,960
[Machine transcript:]
“They don't not want someone to die.”

6
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:17,600
Your father also wants me to die.

7
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:21,020
[Unclear: “Then ... good.”]

8
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:27,120
Once I'm dead, you'll all be happy.

9
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:29,300
Only then can you live.

10
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:33,500
Where would I live?

11
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,140
I want to live together with you.

12
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:38,980
Where will you live?

13
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:44,360
Would you?

14
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:49,680
If I really could live...

15
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:54,860
I would.

16
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,700
I love you.

17
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:07,400
If love requires someone to disappear—
who gets to live?

18
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:09,140
I love you too.

19
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:11,740
So let me kill you.

20
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:19,580
Wouldn't you be sad if you killed me?

21
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:22,280
I would be very...

22
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:24,140
Very happy.

23
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:29,500
Aren't you happy now?

24
00:01:30,140 --> 00:01:30,640
Because of you.

25
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:33,660
You're dead now.

26
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:35,040
I kill you.

27
00:01:35,040 --> 00:01:35,780
Only then can you live.

28
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:38,540
That's how I can be happy.

29
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:40,600
I'm already alive.

30
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,680
Then I'll be happy.

31
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:43,120
Definitely.

32
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:45,200
I'm happy now.

33
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:49,520
You're not happy now.

34
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:56,200
Is this one person's conflict,
or everyone's structure?

35
00:01:56,200 --> 00:02:00,200
[Live action — location sound not transcribed]

36
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:42,200
When positions shift,
who plays “Mother”?

37
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:46,200
[Live action — location sound not transcribed]

38
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:48,200
Who must die
for someone else to live?

39
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:50,340
Don't be afraid.

40
00:05:50,340 --> 00:05:51,720
I see you all...

41
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:54,760
...are still happy.

42
00:05:56,700 --> 00:05:57,320
You all...

43
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:00,840
Because of you, I...

44
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:02,900
That's how I survived.

45
00:06:07,740 --> 00:06:09,600
So are you happy now?

46
00:06:16,340 --> 00:06:17,260
If you...

47
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:19,900
Right now, if you all...

48
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:22,620
If you all do what I say...

49
00:06:22,620 --> 00:06:23,920
I'll be happy.

50
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:24,960
[Machine transcript]
Then you still die.

51
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:28,540
Then...

52
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:28,680
Then...

53
00:06:38,780 --> 00:06:39,980
It seems [someone] died.

54
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:51,200
No answer.
Only the question remains.

